---
title: Lumache with spicy pork sausage ragu
servings: 24
tags: [italian, pork, make-ahead, weekend]
cuisine: italian
source: Lumache, Spicy Pork Sausage Ragù, Whipped Ricotta, Basil by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/lumache
---

> A restaurant batch. The ragu step uses 3.625 kg of sausage, more than one
> batch of the sausage below makes; scale the sausage up or the ragu down.

== Spicy sausage ==

Chill a #meat grinder{} fitted with a medium die. Toss the
@pork shoulder{5%lb}(cubed) with @garlic{50%g} and
@dried calabrian chiles{15%g}, and grind into a bowl.

Grind the @fennel seeds{8%g} and @black peppercorns{10%g} in a
#spice grinder{}. Mix with @kosher salt{20%g}, @Spanish paprika{12%g} and
@cayenne pepper{12%g}, then work into the pork.

Add the @white wine vinegar{40%g} and @water{100%g}(cold) and mix with gloved
hands until sticky. Cover and refrigerate ~{12%hours}.

== Ragu ==

Heat the @extra virgin olive oil{180%g} in a #rondeau{} over medium-high heat.
Brown 3.625 kg of the sausage well, drain off the excess fat, and set the
sausage aside.

Lower the heat. Cook the @onions{850%g}(diced), @carrots{425%g}(diced) and
@celery{425%g}(diced), stirring now and then, until soft. Add
@garlic{50%g}(minced) and cook until fragrant.

Stir in the @tomato paste{150%g} and toast it lightly. Return the sausage and
pour in the @red wine{750%ml}(cabernet sauvignon). Raise to medium and reduce
until the alcohol has cooked off.

Add the @whole peeled plum tomatoes{20%lb}, @dried thyme{8%g},
@dried sage{4%g} and @dried rosemary{2%g}. Bring to a simmer, then cook gently
~{1%hour}, stirring now and then.

Season with @kosher salt{20%g}, @ground black pepper{8%g} and a splash of
@sherry vinegar{}. Keep warm.

== To serve ==

Cook the @lumache{1%lb} in salted boiling water until just al dente. Drain into
a #sauté pan{} with 4 cups of the ragu and toss to coat.

Spoon into shallow bowls, top with @ricotta cheese{4%oz}(whipped) and scatter
with @basil{1%bunch}(torn).
